From a4d1d1ea87c383c30ad8e721f93b18c126556c56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: briansp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 15:52:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cuda: skip the GDN state gather; the sequential kernel reads
 the cache rows (bit-identical)

build_rs gathers each layer's recurrent state with GET_ROWS (1.5 MB per GPU under
-sm tensor) only for GATED_DELTA_NET to read it once.  In the decode/verify band
(single sequence, <= 16 tokens) the graph loop now skips that gather and the
sequential GDN kernel loads its initial state straight from the cache row
s_ids[seq].  The gather is a plain copy, so the values are identical.

The skip requires: the GDN in the same graph, every other reader of the gathered
rows empty, no write to the cache tensor in between, and row ids that outlive the
gather.  The last one needs rs_s_copy flagged as an output (llama-graph) and the
scheduler to keep that flag on its backend copy when n_copies == 1; without it the
allocator reused the ids buffer after the last layer's gather and that layer's
GDN read garbage row ids (aperture violation).

GGML_CUDA_FUSE_GDN_STATE_GATHER=0 restores the gather.

Server A/B (prod settings, 2 rounds, off -> on): greedy 124.2/124.1 -> 125.1/125.2,
chat +0.6-1.4 % on every prompt; greedy sha unchanged, 0 faults.  Trace: state
gather kernels 9576 -> 504 (prefill and multi-sequence batches keep it).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
